cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use lumen, please cite it as below."
title: "lumen: a differentiable optical-photon simulation for neutrino detectors"
abstract: >-
  lumen reads a detector from GDML and traces optical photons through it with Geant4's optical physics, in JAX. It
  records the light that reaches each sensor, turns it into photoelectrons, hit times, charges and PMT waveforms, and
  gives derivatives of those outputs with respect to the detector's optical, sensor and source parameters.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Alterkait
    given-names: Omar
version: 0.1.3
date-released: 2026-11-11
repository-code: "https://github.com/OmarAlterkait/lumen"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - optical photons
  - differentiable simulation
  - JAX
  - Geant4
  - neutrino detectors
  - water Cherenkov
  - liquid argon
